  "id": "rule-learning",
  "term": "rule learning",
  "definition": "Rule learning is the ability to detect a pattern or regularity in a sequence and apply that same pattern to new examples. In infants, this includes recognizing simple structures such as ABA or ABB and generalizing them beyond the specific items originally seen or heard.",
